ota-status on the board, 2026-10-30. Image 005bca6 (which carries ota-status), installed over the air into
slot B and booted; then the hang bundle (fb19ed4-hang) into slot A and left alone for the watchdog to
retire it; then the new bundle into slot A again, looked at before the reboot and after it.
Console capture by the user; the bracketed prefix of the original is the capturing terminal's clock.

=== 1. B running the new image, A the fallback ================================================
# ota-status
Running slot : B   revision 005bca6
Confirmed    : yes, this boot passed its health check
Next boot    : slot B (the running one)
Boot order   : B A
Slot A  /dev/mmcblk0p2   state: STANDBY: good, the fallback if the running slot fails
    attempts  : 3 left, in the boot order: yes
    installed : bundle 6d5dbc6, update number 6 (RAUC's record of the last write)
Slot B  /dev/mmcblk0p3   state: RUNNING, confirmed
    attempts  : 3 left, in the boot order: yes
    revision  : 005bca6 (this image's /etc/build-info)
    installed : bundle 005bca6, update number 5 (RAUC's record of the last write)

=== 2. after three failed boots of the hanging slot A and the fall back to B ===================
# ota-status
Running slot : B   revision 005bca6
Confirmed    : yes, this boot passed its health check
Next boot    : slot B (the running one)
Boot order   : A B
Slot A  /dev/mmcblk0p2   state: RETIRED: it was tried and never confirmed, and is out of boot attempts
    attempts  : 0 left, in the boot order: yes
    installed : bundle fb19ed4-hang, update number 7 (RAUC's record of the last write)
Slot B  /dev/mmcblk0p3   state: RUNNING, confirmed          (attempts 3 left, installed bundle 005bca6, update number 5)

=== 3. the new bundle installed into A, not yet rebooted ========================================
